---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | ShipToCash"
  description="Peng Zhou writes ShipToCash — practical guides that take vibe coders from localhost to a live, earning app."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-8">About ShipToCash</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6 not-prose mb-8">
        <img
          src={SITE.avatar}
          alt={`${SITE.author}, founder of ShipToCash`}
          width="112"
          height="112"
          loading="lazy"
          class="rounded-full shadow-md flex-shrink-0"
          style="width: 112px; height: 112px;"
        />
        <div class="flex-1">
          <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink-900 mb-1">{SITE.author}</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-3">Vibe coder &middot; Founder of ShipToCash</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Hi, I'm Peng Zhou. I build small software products, and I write about the
        unglamorous part nobody teaches you: getting an app actually <em>deployed</em>,
        taking real money from real users, and not getting into legal trouble doing it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I ship on Cloudflare Pages with auto-deploy from GitHub — it's the setup I use for
        everything. A big part of what I write about is the gap Stripe doesn't cover: how do you
        actually get paid when Stripe won't open an account in your country? I dig into the
        workarounds — Ko-fi, PayPal, Paddle — and the tax and payout trade-offs nobody explains
        up front. The goal is the same for every guide here: take you from "it runs on my laptop"
        to "strangers are paying me for this."
      </p>
      <p>
        Every guide here is something I've actually done, on the current version of the tool.
        If a step is missing a screenshot, it's because I forgot to take one — not because I'm
        hand-waving the hard part.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also write about AI tools over at
        <a
          href="https://aikitguides.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">AI Kit Guides</a>
        — same person, different lane. If you're still picking the tools themselves, that's a
        good place to start.
      </p>

      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Deploy</strong> — hosting, domains, HTTPS, databases</li>
        <li><strong>Payments</strong> — Stripe, Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, taxes (and what to do when Stripe says no)</li>
        <li><strong>Monetize</strong> — ads, subscriptions, pricing</li>
        <li><strong>Legal</strong> — privacy policies, GDPR, terms</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Found a broken step? Built something with one of these guides? I'd love to hear about it.
        The fastest way to reach me is on
        <a
          href={SITE.github}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">GitHub</a>,
        or through the <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
